  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Show that $3x^2-4x+2>0$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$3x^2-4x+2=3\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)^2+\\frac23\\geq\\frac23>0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x^2-4x+2&=3\\left(x^2-\\frac43x\\right)+2\\\\3x^2-4x+2&=3\\left(x^2-\\frac43x+\\frac49-\\frac49\\right)+2\\\\3x^2-4x+2&=3\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)^2-\\frac43+2\\\\3x^2-4x+2&=3\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)^2+\\frac23\\\\3x^2-4x+2&\\geq\\frac23>0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe square is non-negative for every real $x$, so the expression is positive for every real $x$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
